{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"THE THIN VERTICAL SLICE IS GREEN LIVE. The filter fix was the last defect.\n\nRUN: 30704452033, job 91381036654 (\"jira DC harness smoke\") — SUCCESS.\n`[jira-live-canary] collected=25 executed=25 skipped=0` / `25 passed in 466.58s`.\n\nALL FIVE CELLS PASSED:\n  * test_the_working_repo_is_isolated_from_this_project\n  * test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed\n  * test_the_inbound_create_is_PLANNED_for_a_new_dc_issue\n  * test_a_dc_issue_reaches_the_local_store_inbound   <- had failed FOUR times\n  * test_the_scrubbed_copy_plans_no_deletions_or_outbound_updates\n\nskipped=0 matters: a live cell with no harness SKIPS rather than fails, so a skip would be no\nevidence at all. All 25 executed against a real Jira 8.17.1 Data Center instance.\n\nWHAT IS NOW PROVEN, over a copy of this project's ACTUAL ticket store (2673 tickets, count\nmatching `git ls-tree origin/tickets` exactly — a comparison, not a `> 0` floor, so a PARTIAL\nextraction would fail):\n  * isolation, asserted not assumed: NO git remote on BOTH the outer repo AND the\n    `.tickets-tracker/` store repo (the one `sync.remote` would actually push),\n    REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off, no Cloud credential in the environment;\n  * the scrub leaves zero `.bridge_state*` artifacts, and the store repo's history is created\n    AFTER the scrub so the bindings are absent from history too;\n  * a dry-run over the scrubbed copy plans ZERO deletions and ZERO outbound updates — the live\n    confirmation of the reasoning that an outbound UPDATE cannot be emitted without a binding;\n  * the inbound differ PLANS a create for a new DC issue (unfiltered dry-run), and\n  * a DC-created issue REACHES THE LOCAL STORE. **Inbound is proven over a real store copy**, not\n    over an empty one.\n\nTHE FOUR DEFECTS THIS COST, each real and each a different cause — worth keeping because the\nsingle \"the ticket did not appear\" assertion made every one of them look like the same failure:\n 1. `dc_transport` was module-local to test_transport.py, so it was invisible to a sibling module\n    (ERROR at setup). Moved to conftest. NOTE `--collect-only` cannot catch this — fixtures\n    resolve at SETUP; `pytest --fixtures <module>` can.\n 2. The store copy was not a git repo. `.tickets-tracker/` IS its own repo on the orphan `tickets`\n    branch and the reconciler commits into it directly, so every store write failed with\n    CalledProcessError(128).\n 3. MY WRONG GUESS: index lag. I added a poll, it did not fire, and inbound_differ still reported\n    0 — so the hypothesis was disproven by its own fix. The poll is kept (it is correct, and the\n    pagination cell needs it) but it was never the cause here.\n 4. THE ACTUAL CAUSE: `--filter-local-ids` could not match the inbound create.\n    `_build_filter_target_set` (reconcile_helpers.py:419-434) seeds the target set with the passed\n    strings verbatim and can only add a Jira key via `binding_store.get_jira_key(lid)` — a binding\n    that does not exist for an issue arriving inbound for the first time. An inbound create's\n    `target` IS the Jira key, so `RBJ...-1 ∉ {jira-rbj...-1}` and it was dropped. Fixed by passing\n    BOTH identifiers; no product change needed, because the matcher already tests `target`,\n    `provenance.local_id` and `provenance.jira_key`, and the parser splits on commas\n    (`__main__.py:682`).\n\nAND THE DIAGNOSTIC LESSON THAT ENDED IT: splitting \"is the create PLANNED\" from \"is it APPLIED\"\ninto two cells localised the fault on the FIRST run after four blind attempts. `inbound_differ\ntotal=0` is printed POST-FILTER, so it never meant what it appeared to mean.\n\nCARRY INTO THE OUTBOUND WORK: the plan's `bound_dc_issue` step 2 specifies filtering on\n`jira-<dc_key.lower()>` alone. That is insufficient for exactly the reason above and MUST pass the\nDC key too, or all 14 outbound UPDATE cells will fail the same way."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785596824141299001,"uuid":"b053145e-37b3-4ac2-b3be-383e78fa7e7a"}